{
  "schema": "mitts.jersey.v2",
  "description": "Mitts fruit league - one team per slot, each with home and away kits. Stripes are procedural horizontal bands over a UV region: pos = band center (0=top of region, 1=bottom), width = band height as a fraction of the region, both 0..1. Stripes paint in array order (later over earlier). Centered cross-section bands = stack stripes sharing pos with shrinking widths, widest first (Lime, Pomegranate, Pineapple). Stacked bands = adjacent stripes edge to edge (Watermelon's slice edge, Peach's sunset). Asymmetric slices offset a band's pos off-center (Dragonfruit seed-line). For a cross-section to show its outer color, set the region base to that color so it reads as the skin/rind edges. Uniform lettering is text.color, bordered on the sweater by text.stroke when set (optional; absent = no border); shoulders.stroke borders the shoulder numbers the same way. text.outline is a separate color, the outline UI chrome (off-screen indicators) draws around the number. jersey.collar (optional, falls back to yoke) = the ring around the neck; jersey.yoke (optional, falls back to the jersey base) = the top of the shoulders, from the collar over the top of each shoulder cap; shoulders.color = the rest of the cap, the patch at the top of the arm carrying the number. arms.elbow (optional) = the elbow pad, which otherwise takes the forearm's color at the elbow and disappears into the sleeve. primary/secondary/light are the team's UI palette (HUD, lobby cards, scorebug headers): home cards render as primary body + secondary stripe, away cards as light body + primary stripe. light mirrors the away kit's jersey base (the away body color) so the UI away card matches the 3D away sweater. ui_ink (optional) letters both UI sides instead of light/primary, for a team whose primary contrasts with neither white text nor a white card (Lemon, Pineapple, Lime). These drive UI only; the home/away kit blocks below drive the 3D uniform meshes. goalie_pads is the goalie's pads, blocker and trapper, white in every bundled kit; his trim on them is the team's primary, or its secondary where the primary is too faint on the pads.",
